> improved and is now detecting a real underlying issue affecting the
> broader R ecosystem on riscv64 (<https://wiki.debian.org/R/riscv64>).
>
> Is there a way to mark this test failure as “not a regression” so that
> it doesn’t block migration to Testing?

You can mark the autopkgtests of r-cran-sparsevctrs so that they are
not run on riscv64 by adding the following to debian/tests/control:

Architecture: !riscv64

Another way is to patch the affected tests so that they are skipped,
or pass, on riscv64.

Regards
Graham

