Hi Mechtilde,

in the r-cran-* packages that go to the NEW queue, the whole content of
the debian/ directory is script-generated.  All the creative work goes
in packages like dh-r, routine-update, uscan or cme.

Also, if group authorship is not possible in Debian, we may need to
wonder how to handle group authorship when it is done upstream.  In
particular, in the R community there is a trend that when a package
"foo" declares a MIT license, the only copyright information given
is something like: "Copyright: the <foo> authors".

I would be grateful to be allowed to do the same.  I have updated a lot
of copyright files of r-cran-* packages.  Upstream and Debian licenses
eventually drift.  I want to empower the future package uploaders to
adjust the Debian license without me being a bottleneck.

Cheers,

Charles

