From plessy at debian.org  Mon May 11 01:29:33 2026
From: plessy at debian.org (Charles Plessy)
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 10:29:33 +0900
Subject: Debhelper merge request to not re-compress .RData, .rda and .rds files.
Message-ID: <agEw_S1OUu2Yc6md@kumo.plessy.net>

Hi all,

this is a quick note to tell you that I opened a merge request on debhelper
so that dh_compress skips files ending in .[Rr]da, .[Rr][Dd]ata or .[Rr]ds,
because by default they are already compressed.

https://salsa.debian.org/debian/debhelper/-/merge_requests/157

If accepted, the change might break some scripts that attempt to uncompress
these files before use.  This said, the re-compression status of these files in
our packages is not stable across upstream updates anyway since dh_compress
also applies a size filter, therefore the scripts accessing these files need
anyway to account for that uncertaincy.  Once the merge request accepted this
uncertaincy will be gone.

Please let me know if you have objections based on the above or other comments.

Have a nice day,

Charles

